{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Benjamin, a wolf that tears prey.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): he likened Benjamin to a wolf that seizes, because the children of Benjamin are destined to seize, as it is said (Judges 21:21): ״וחטפתם לכם איש אשתו״." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> ״בנימין זאב יטרף״ — Benjamin had ten sons, equal to the numerical value of זאב. <b>In the morning he devours prey.</b> This is Saul son of Kish, who is of the tribe of Benjamin, who was the first king and was the beginning of Israel's kingdom. <b>And at evening he divides the spoil.</b> Even when the sun of Israel sets through Nebuchadnezzar, who exiles them to Babylon, he shall divide spoil: Mordecai and Esther, who are of the children of Benjamin, shall divide the spoil of Haman, as it is said (Esther 8:7): ״הנה בית המן נתתי לאסתר״." "<b>And by way of the Kabbalah:</b> ״בנימין זאב יטרף״ — Benjamin was comprised of two attributes through which the entire structure is comprised and bound, above and below; and so the Shekhinah that dwells in his portion is comprised of all. And they likened him to a wolf that tears, eating continually — of the morning and continually of the between-the-evenings. And because he is comprised of the ten, he begot sons equal to their number and corresponding to them; and this is the expression ״יחלק שלל״ — divides spoil — in the manner of (Psalms 68:13): ״ונות בית תחלק שלל״, and this is the Shekhinah. And from this Onkelos translated (ארעיה תשרי שכינתיה) — in his land the Shekhinah dwells. And understand this." "<b>And after</b> I have explained to you here, and also in the pericope of the birth of the tribes, that each one of them is named for a specific attribute among the attributes of the Holy One, blessed be He, you will further find, if you open the eye of your understanding, that the twelve stones of the breastplate, in which the twelve tribes are fixed and engraved — the colors of those stones correspond to the colors of their attributes above. For Reuben, who alludes to the attribute of judgment, his stone is אדם (carnelian); and Benjamin, who is comprised of all the attributes, his stone is ישפה (jasper), which is comprised of many colors. And in the verse ״ועשית חשן משפט״ I shall mention this, with the help of Heaven, and there you shall see it."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:21:50.984779240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}